C R152 OL DEP-002,DEP-011,ARC-020 | MUST | Use the approved technology from the decision register and a conditional technology only when its capability is now needed; a new major library or framework, or a replacement of an approved technology, is Reserved — stop with a Decision Request. | Dependency additions | none stated
C R153 OL DEP-020 | DEFAULT | When resilience is required prefer Microsoft.Extensions.Http.Resilience for HttpClient and Microsoft.Extensions.Resilience for general pipelines; a direct Polly reference or Polly API configuration is an explicit exception needing a documented reason why the Microsoft.Extensions APIs cannot express the requirement. | Resilience packages | documented exception
C R154 OL DEP-017 | DEFAULT | When Controller API versioning has been explicitly adopted use the Controller integration of Asp.Versioning (e.g. Asp.Versioning.Mvc with Asp.Versioning.Mvc.ApiExplorer); do not add it before versioning is adopted. | API-versioning package | none stated
C X18 EX DEP-010,DEP-004 | MUST | Register FluentValidation validators with FluentValidation.DependencyInjectionExtensions; do not add a deprecated or legacy ASP.NET automatic-validation integration package without a concrete requirement. | Validation package choice | concrete requirement (but FluentValidation.AspNetCore is a hard manifest error, X9) | DEP-010 makes FluentValidation the standard library but prescribes no registration package; no oracle policy restricts the automatic-validation integration package. | Validators are registered through the DI-extensions package; FluentValidation.AspNetCore is not added.
C R155 OL DEP-003 | MUST | For every NuGet or npm addition or update determine the latest stable version compatible with target framework/runtime and peers, verify it from the registry (not memory, examples or older content) and avoid prerelease or floating versions unless explicitly requested; 'latest' means latest stable compatible. | Dependency additions/updates | explicit request
C R156 OL DEP-004 | MUST | Before installation check, for the exact selected version, deprecation status, known vulnerabilities from advisory data and the license from official registry metadata (and upstream text when necessary); permissive licenses are generally suitable; free download does not make a package acceptable. | Dependency additions/updates | none stated
C R157 OL DEP-005 | REQUIRES_APPROVAL | Paid/commercial packages are not installed automatically: present explicit choices with reasonable free alternatives (or say none exist), never substitute silently; strong copyleft, dual licensing, source-available/custom or unclear licenses are not adopted automatically — explain the concern and alternatives; no legal conclusions beyond the published license. | Dependency additions | none stated
C R158 OL DEP-006 | MUST | NuGet installs add the version to Directory.Packages.props and a versionless PackageReference to the narrowest project that needs it. | NuGet installation | none stated
C R159 OL DEP-007 | MUST | npm installs go into the Angular workspace with the right category (--save-dev for build/test tooling) and keep package-lock.json consistent. | npm installation | none stated
C R160 OL DEP-025 | MUST NOT | Never use --force or --legacy-peer-deps merely to bypass incompatible peer dependencies; resolve the actual compatibility problem. | npm installation | none stated
C R161 OL WF-005,WF-007 | MUST | After a dependency change restore and build the affected projects and run check-dependencies. | Dependency changes | none stated
C R162 OL DEP-004,GOV-014 | MUST | Inspect vulnerability information (dotnet package list --vulnerable --include-transitive; npm audit) with context; do not upgrade or replace unrelated packages because of a finding. | Dependency changes | none stated
C X19 EX DEP-001,GOV-014 | MUST | Remove a dependency that is no longer used when that is part of the current change and safe to verify; do not leave dead references behind. | Changes that make a dependency unused | Not during unrelated cleanup of a narrowly scoped task. | No oracle policy obliges removing packages made unused by a change (RUN-010 concerns only unused usings). | A change that stops using a package must also remove its references.
C R163 OL GOV-014 | MUST NOT | Do not perform unrelated dependency cleanup during a narrowly scoped task. | Dependency changes | none stated
C X20 EX DEP-004,DEP-005,WF-009 | MUST | The add-dependency output reports package, selected version and why, license, deprecation and vulnerability status, approval obtained (if needed), files changed and the verification result. | End of add-dependency | none stated | WF-009 covers verification reporting only; the per-package report content is an additional workflow duty. | Every dependency change report must state license and due-diligence status.
C R164 OL DEP-014,DEP-015,GOV-012 | DEFAULT | Use Angular Material components consistently for common UI primitives where they meet the requirement; wrap a Material component in a custom abstraction only for a concrete reason. | Angular UI | concrete reason
C R165 OL WF-016 | DEFAULT | When OpenAPI client generation is adopted keep generated code separate from handwritten feature logic and regenerate it when the API contract changes. | Angular API clients | none stated
C R166 OL TST-003,TST-002,DEP-014 | SHOULD | Frontend test targets are meaningful component behavior, validation, data-access request mapping, important route/auth behavior and complex reactive state, not Angular framework internals; run the workspace's configured test runner; E2E covers a small number of important workflows unless more is required; the same behavior is not duplicated at every level. | Angular testing | none stated
C R167 OL RUN-001 | DEFAULT | Start with route lazy loading and sensible rendering and data access; specialized memoization, virtual scrolling or custom change-detection work follows an identified need. | Angular performance | none stated
