C X23 EX GOV-017,GOV-007 | MUST (conditional) | When rationale, alternatives or consequences need more than the register sentence add an ADR docs/decisions/NNNN-<slug>.md (Status, Date, Register, Context, Decision, Alternatives considered, Consequences) cited in Details in; superseding marks the old ADR 'Superseded by NNNN' and replaces the register entry — never two active entries for one choice; register IDs are stable and never reused. | Recording decisions | none stated | No oracle policy requires ADRs, ADR structure or superseding bookkeeping. | A consequential decision needing explanation must get an ADR in the fixed template.
